Subject: [PATCH 06/12] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 6;
 built on 5c7abd72a with the ten patches of series 4, the move of the old
 front pages and the first five of series 5 applied): A FILE THAT IS TRACKED
 COMPRESSED IS HELD TO WHAT IT HOLDS (main's M9, from the second round of
 Review 79; register row P-812). The census of B1786 is tracked compressed.
 Its list records the hash of the content, under the name the content has when
 it is unpacked. No tracked file has that name, so the entry stood as one that
 names no tracked file, frozen in that state, and the compressed file could be
 replaced unseen. Planted by the seat as main wrote it, on main's 22808aa3f
 and on the series: the content replaced and committed, the gate passes. THE
 MEND: where a list names no tracked file, and one file is tracked under that
 name with a suffix of compression, the entry is held to what that file holds.
 The gate unpacks it as it reads and hashes what comes out; the same content
 packed again with other bytes verifies; a file that cannot be unpacked as its
 name says, or that unpacks to more than a bound, is not hashed in part and
 fails the gate, which does not hang. Of the 2,250 entries on main one is of
 this kind, and it verifies: 1,830 verify where 1,829 did. Its key is taken
 out of the table of entries that do not verify, in this patch, and the
 table's pinned hash is changed with it: the table may only shorten, and it
 holds 416. THIS TURNS ONE TEST OF MAIN'S LOCK FOR B1880 RED, BY THAT LOCK'S
 OWN DESIGN: it holds the table to 417 keys and to the hash recorded in the
 arc's own file, so that the lock is told when the table moves. The arc's
 record and its lock are main's to change at the landing: 416 keys, and the
 hash that this patch pins in the gates. One line of main's test of the gate
 in tests/ held the table to 417 keys as well; it now holds it to 416, with a
 dated note. The gate takes seven tenths of a second longer on this machine:
 the census unpacks to 127 megabytes. What it does not reach: a compressed
 file that no list names; an archive of several files. The lock: three tests
 added to tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py, for three kinds of
 compression. On the commit before, all three fail: the content replaced
 passes the gate, a file that cannot be unpacked passes it, and on this
 repository no entry reads the compressed file. Tested against planted errors;
 reproduced, the part main had run; computed once. 0 of 19.

